[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2916549309","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106902#issuecomment-2916549309","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106902","id":2916549309,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6t1wK9","user":{"login":"RedMser","id":5117197,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTcxOTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5117197?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser","html_url":"https://github.com/RedMser","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-28T14:23:52Z","updated_at":"2025-05-28T14:23:52Z","body":"Does this in any way affect the scripting-exposed `ConfigFile` class? It's hard for me to tell from looking at the code.\r\n\r\n> use lines starting with =, which are currently ignored, to include the path-to-uid mapping information\r\n\r\nEek... I can see why you did it this way, but I really hope there would be a better solution to this.\r\n\r\nFor example you could be adding a format version field to the `ConfigFile` format - compatibility is retained since we can just treat a missing version field as version 1.\r\nThis would also be useful in the future, for example if we add more Variant types.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godoteng